  "content": {
    "id": "p7-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Find the equation of the normal to $y=3\\sin(2x)$ at the point where $x=\\frac{\\pi}{8}$ in exact general form.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$8x+24\\sqrt{2}\\,y-72-\\pi=0$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx}&=6\\cos(2x)\\end{aligned}$$\n\nAt $x=\\frac{\\pi}{8}$:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx}&=6\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\\\&=6\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\\\&=3\\sqrt{2}.\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}m_{\\text{normal}}&=-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}\\\\&=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}.\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\nAt $x=\\frac{\\pi}{8}$:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}y&=3\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\nThe normal is\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}y-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}&=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}\\left(x-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)\\\\24\\sqrt{2}\\,y-72&=-8x+\\pi\\\\8x+24\\sqrt{2}\\,y-72-\\pi&=0.\n\\end{aligned}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 50
